WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.040
The new trailer for Pet Sematary suggests
one major change from the novel and one major

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:05.950
change from the 1989 movie.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:10.250
If you haven’t seen trailer #2 yet -- I’d
recommend not watching it, you can just watch

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:14.110
this Things You Missed video, and I’ll tell
you when to leave if you want to avoid spoilers.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:15.110
Deal?

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:16.110
Deal.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:19.230
Let’s roll the intro.

00:00:20.789 --> 00:00:24.150
So the trailer opens with the mother of the
family, Rachel, telling her husband that their

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:28.340
daughter Ellie discovered a “charming landmark”
in woods and then it shows Ellie wandering

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.290
around the Pet Sematary by herself.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.480
This is not how it goes down in the book at
all.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.030
In the book, their neighbor Jud Crandall takes
the entire Creed family to the Pet Sematary

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.420
to introduce them to the woods behind their
house.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:42.780
Maybe that does still happen, because we do
see both of them there together later in the

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.789
trailer, and trailers have been known to lie
to us in the past.

00:00:45.789 --> 00:00:49.600
But when we do see Ellie supposedly arriving
at the Pet Sematary, there’s a little picture

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.449
frame in the bottom right corner with a photo
of a parrot.

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:55.949
When they first visit the Pet Sematary in
the book, Ellie’s father, Louis, notices

00:00:55.949 --> 00:00:59.819
a grave plot labeled Polynesia and thinks
to himself that Polynesia would have been

00:00:59.819 --> 00:01:03.699
a parrot if he remembered his Dr. Doolittle
correctly and would have squaked her last

00:01:03.699 --> 00:01:06.720
“Polly want a cracker” in the summer of
1953.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:10.470
King also describes Polynesia’s grave when
Louis returns to the burial ground towards

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:14.680
the end of the book and when he steps over
the ragged chunk of board that marks Polynesia’s

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:18.540
final resting place; it kind of represents
him going past the land of the dead.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:22.560
Also, if you go frame by frame while the headstones
are flashing on screen, you can read this

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.290
one, labeled Trixie, kilt on the highway,
which is also one of the grave markers Louis

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:29.920
reads when first visiting the Pet Sematary
in the book, where he also sees the death

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.390
date September 15, 1968.

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:35.470
So I think it’s pretty cool that they’re
referencing some of the Pet Sematary animal

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:38.200
inhabitants in the movie, nice little easter
eggs.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.851
One thing that’s included in the movie that
is not in the book is this mask left on one

00:01:41.851 --> 00:01:45.030
of the graves, and these kids wearing the
masks as they parade their deceased pets to

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:46.030
the sematary.

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:49.000
There is a story that Jud Crandall passes
down in the book about how the kids would

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.130
bring their pets down the forest path to the
sematary.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:56.060
Sometimes the pet owner would go alone, like
when Jud buried his dog Spot, and sometimes

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:59.420
they would have more of a funeral procession
type of thing, I specifically remember Jud

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:03.090
telling of an argument between two kids back
in the day getting into a debate about who

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:04.630
got to hold onto the casket.

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:07.960
But the animal masks and instruments were
never a part of the book.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:11.540
There are some things that were mentioned
in the book, but after being absent from the

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:13.969
80s film have returned for the new adaptation.

00:02:13.969 --> 00:02:15.370
Let’s roll the clip.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:18.020
“It’s not some campfire story.”

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.440
“Saw these in the trees up there.”

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.080
“They’re warnings.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:25.740
The local tribes carved them before they fled.”

00:02:25.749 --> 00:02:31.150
Louis researches the spiral in this book called
Modern History of Eastern Native Tribes.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:35.159
The caption here says, “The pictograph of
the spiral was found carved into the trees

00:02:35.159 --> 00:02:39.560
of the forests of Maine, As a warning to others,
or a way of warding off the evil spirit.”

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:40.769
What is this evil spirit?

00:02:40.769 --> 00:02:44.540
It’s right there: the Wendigo, an Algonquian
mythological creature.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.890
(In the case of Pet Sematary it’s referred
to as a Micmac legend).

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:52.379
The Wendigo has ties to cannibalism and greed
in times of famine and resides in the northeast

00:02:52.379 --> 00:02:53.930
region of the US.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:57.409
Some versions of the legend say a human who
craves another man’s flesh is cursed to

00:02:57.409 --> 00:03:01.500
become a Wendigo, but the Wendigo in Stephen
King’s novel is more of a deity who stalks

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.900
the ground of Ludlow, Maine where the story
takes place.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:08.069
Jud tells Louis that the Micmac tribe stopped
using their burial ground, because the ground

00:03:08.069 --> 00:03:09.590
had been “soured” by the Wendigo.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:13.480
He also blames the Wendigo for causing bad
things to happen in the town, telling Louis

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:17.640
he believes that Wendigo possessed him to
show Louis the Micmac burial ground.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:21.209
Legend has it that if the creature touches
you, it can turn you into a cannibal.

00:03:21.209 --> 00:03:25.099
The pictures shown in the trailer show off
the Wendigo’s cannibalistic side and it’s

00:03:25.099 --> 00:03:28.609
form which matches the typical depiction of
the Wendigo with a human body capped by the

00:03:28.609 --> 00:03:30.010
head or horns of a stag.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:33.640
The spiral is also mentioned in the book,
but it’s more of a sign of the Wendigo’s

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:36.829
intervention and introduction of ideas that
go against nature.

00:03:36.829 --> 00:03:40.629
When Louis visits Pleasantview Cemetery, he
finds himself thinking about the graves at

00:03:40.629 --> 00:03:41.629
the Pet Sematary.

00:03:41.629 --> 00:03:44.810
He refers to the spiral as the oldest sign
of power in the world.

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:49.299
Man’s oldest symbol of that twisty bridge
that may exist between the world and the gulf.

00:03:49.299 --> 00:03:53.659
Louis finds himself absentmindedly drawing
a spiral pattern in the dirt while he is thinking

00:03:53.659 --> 00:03:55.309
and erases it before leaving.

00:03:55.309 --> 00:03:59.349
Then, later on, when he returns to the burial
ground, he notices that the rocks have fallen

00:03:59.349 --> 00:04:03.150
in such a way as to give to appearance of
a gigantic spiral, giving us the idea that

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.849
a greater presence is at work.

00:04:04.849 --> 00:04:08.739
On one of the other pages of the book, someone
has drawn in their own spiral and a pentagram,

00:04:08.739 --> 00:04:12.590
I’m guessing Louis finds his hands drawing
in these symbols without realizing just as

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:14.730
he drew the spiral on the dirt in the book.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:18.829
Jud Crandall is seen wearing a hat throughout
several scenes of the trailer that says LeVett

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:19.889
Motor Oil.

00:04:19.889 --> 00:04:24.490
This might be an oil company based near Fort
LeVett in Maine, which is named after Christopher

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:27.020
LeVett, one of the early settlers of the New
England area.

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:30.990
I think Jud wearing this hat means that he
represents the white man laying down a path

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:34.050
into Native American territory that they have
no business meddling in.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:38.620
Jud is the one to show Louis how to get to
the Mic Mac burial ground and introduce him

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:40.020
to the power it holds.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:43.370
Native American curses are a common theme
in Stephen King’s stories.

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:46.730
And speaking of King’s writing, it looks
like there’s a little reference to Carrie,

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:49.120
with a hand reaching out of the ground and
grabbing Louis’s arm.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:52.780
And that’s not something from the book,
so I’d guess it’s part of Louis’s dream.

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:55.729
One thing that was not shown in the first
trailer that has been revealed here in the

00:04:55.729 --> 00:05:00.050
second one is Zelda, Rachel’s sister who
passed away when they were young from severe

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:01.200
spinal meningitis.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:06.360
The thought of Zelda haunts Rachel for the
rest of her life and she even has visions

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:10.650
of her as an adult, which appears to be what’s
going on in this scene and it looks pretty

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:11.650
horrifying.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:15.590
We also get a better look at Louis’s encounter
with Victor Pascow, a University student that

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:19.270
dies under Louis’s care during his first
day of work and tries to warn him about the

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:21.450
evil that lies beyond the Pet Sematary.

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:23.710
In the book he was hit by a car while out
jogging.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:26.680
It looks like they’ve changed things up
a bit in this new movie, because he’s not

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.160
wearing running shorts and something is sticking
out of his neck, can’t really tell what.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:34.039
I don’t know why this change was made, and
that kind of leads me to my next point, however,

00:05:34.039 --> 00:05:37.740
if you don’t want any spoilers this is the
end of the line for you.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:41.020
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring the deathbell for

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:43.430
notifications and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:45.080
Go watch this video.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:48.610
If you’re still here, you may have already
thought what I’m thinking: that Pascow’s

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:51.350
injury seems to just be changed for change’s
sake.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:55.189
We won’t know for sure until we see the
movie, but as of right now it certainly seems

00:05:55.189 --> 00:05:56.189
that way.

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:59.849
You’ve probably also noticed that the trailer
seems to suggest that Ellie is going to be

00:05:59.849 --> 00:06:03.470
the one struck down by the truck, as opposed
to her brother Gage.

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:07.650
Like I said before, trailers do lie sometimes,
but it does seem like Ellie is seen running

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:11.220
into the road before the truck comes, there
are Ellie sized footprints on the stairs,

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:14.460
and Ellie tracks mud into the house and horrifies
her mother with her appearance.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:19.159
Then and as Rachel is watching over Gage,
something pops up and scares her, and it appears

00:06:19.159 --> 00:06:20.159
to be Ellie.

00:06:20.159 --> 00:06:23.919
At the end of the trailer, a girl with a cat
mask attacks Jud, which may or may not be

00:06:23.919 --> 00:06:27.590
Ellie, but a lot of signs seem to point to
her being the one Louis has to bury in the

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:28.880
cursed burial ground.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:30.919
So why was this changed in the remake?

00:06:30.919 --> 00:06:34.930
In my personal opinion, this would have been
a fun change if it had been for shock value.

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:38.539
Fans of the originals would go into the movie
expecting it to be Gage who is killed, making

00:06:38.539 --> 00:06:41.970
it that much more shocking when Ellie is unexpectedly
struck down.

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:45.069
But now that they’ve gone and spoiled it
in the trailer... that won’t be the case

00:06:45.069 --> 00:06:49.159
at all -- which makes me think it’s just
another example of change for the sake of

00:06:49.159 --> 00:06:50.159
change.

00:06:50.159 --> 00:06:54.039
Maybe there is some reason that the roles
of Ellie and Gage are flipped in the film,

00:06:54.039 --> 00:06:57.490
and I won’t make my final judgements until
I have seen the movie, but if they are just

00:06:57.490 --> 00:07:01.349
changing it for no reason, then some of the
brilliance of the story is going to be lost.

00:07:01.349 --> 00:07:05.150
For example, the contrast between Louis’s
first trip, where he struggles to carry Gage

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:09.169
in the baby backpack and his second trip where
he easily carries Gage’s corpse in the middle

00:07:09.169 --> 00:07:12.699
of the night is going to be lost because it’s
not like he’ll be carrying Ellie during

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:14.360
the first trip in the movie.

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:19.120
And the psychological trauma Gage’s death
puts on Ellie won’t be there with Gage in the movie,

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:23.110
because he’s just not old enough to fully
comprehend it like Ellie would have.

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:26.590
We will just have to wait and see how everything
shakes out, but let me know what you think

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:31.080
of these changes so far and make sure you’re
subscribed to CZsWorld and ring the deathbell

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:35.379
so you don’t miss out on Things You Missed
episodes on the the 1989 Pet Sematary, it’s

00:07:35.379 --> 00:07:39.599
sequel and more Pet Sematary related content
coming soon to this channel.

00:07:39.599 --> 00:07:41.350
I’ll see you in the next one.

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:43.529
Assuming we both survive.

